Product-specific custom components create refurbishment bottlenecks where spare part availability becomes limiting factors. Standardized parts reduce refurbishment lead times and costs through competitive sourcing. Standard parts support distributed refurbishment networks and independent refurbishers who cannot maintain diverse custom part inventories.

Commodity parts create transparent pricing and quality competition. Standard part specifications enable future manufacturer independence if original suppliers discontinue products. Wide spare parts availability extends refurbishment viability far beyond manufacturing company timelines.